2026-10-20T14:41:19.957044Z TRACE tungstenite::protocol: Received message {"type": "response.output_item.done", "sequence_number": 389, "output_index": 1, "item": {"type": "message", "id": "msg_06efd4d206f98dd3016ad77d8cbe54819aaee7cc73d72a9462", "metadata": {"turn_id": "01a159c2-13f8-7180-9ddc-756488d5e917"}, "internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough": {"create_time": 1792507276.7483797, "turn_id": "01a159c2-13f8-7180-9ddc-756488d5e917"}, "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "content": [{"type": "output_text", "text": "At dawn, the river gathers light before the valley does. It carries a pale ribbon of sky between alder roots, polished stones, and fields still silver with dew. Mist drifts above the current, loosening slowly as swallows cross from bank to bank. Nothing seems hurried, yet everything moves.\n\nUpstream, snowmelt enters through narrow creeks, cold enough to numb a hand. Farther down, rainwater slips from forests, stained amber by leaves and earth. Each tributary brings its own memory: mountain shadow, pasture mud, fallen needles, the faint mineral taste of rock. The river accepts them without argument and becomes larger than any source.\n\nPeople meet it in different ways. An angler stands knee deep beside a gravel bar, reading small disturbances on the surface. Children launch sticks from a wooden bridge and race downstream to watch them pass beneath. A farmer opens a gate before sunrise, guiding a measured share toward thirsty rows. In town, walkers pause along the embankment, drawn by the steady sound beneath traffic.\n\nThe river also keeps harder histories. Flood marks remain on warehouse bricks. Rusted bolts show where an old mill wheel turned. Beneath a quiet bend lie branches, bottles, coins, and perhaps names no map records. Water covers these things, but does not erase them. It carries traces forward, breaking them into stories too scattered to recover.\n\nBy evening, the river darkens first. Cottonwoods become silhouettes, and windows along the shore kindle one by one. The current holds each reflection briefly, stretching gold into trembling lines, then releases it. Beyond the last houses, it bends through reeds and disappears.\n\nStill, disappearance is only distance. The river continues under stars, joining wider water, bearing cold, silt, seeds, and moonlight toward a sea it has never seen. There, its long journey ends and another restless journey begins.\n\n2", "annotations": [], "logprobs": []}], "phase": "final_answer"}}
